# =============================================================================
#  PetPal — 3DS UI strings  ·  English (en)  ·  SOURCE LOCALE
# =============================================================================
#  This file lists every player-facing text string in the 3DS app so it can be
#  translated into other languages. To make a translation, copy this file to
#  "3DS_strings_<code>.lang" (e.g. 3DS_strings_FR.lang) and translate the values.
#
#  HOW TO TRANSLATE — please read:
#   • Translate ONLY the text to the RIGHT of the first '=' on each line.
#   • Do NOT change the KEY on the left of '=' — it is how the app finds the
#     string and is the SAME in every language. Keys also tell you where the
#     text appears (AREA.NAME) and where it comes from (see "# src:" notes).
#   • Keep every {placeholder} EXACTLY as written — the app swaps in a name or
#     number at runtime. You MAY move a {placeholder} to fit your grammar, but
#     keep all of them and don't translate the word inside the braces.
#     Each placeholder is explained in a "# ph:" note above the line.
#   • Keep \n as a line break. Keep leading/trailing spaces you see.
#   • Lines starting with '#' are notes for translators and are ignored by tools.
#   • The 3DS font is limited; prefer plain Latin text and keep lines short —
#     button hints fit ~8 chars, status lines ~40 chars on the top screen.
#
#  Not included here (intentionally): developer/diagnostic text (the CECD
#  self-test line, debug "test pass" tools) and the profanity bl/filter list in
#  source/util/NameFilter.cpp (that is a moderation word-list, not UI copy — a
#  full localization would supply its own per-language list separately).
# =============================================================================


